    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four things, stated plainly so you know which parts of this page are reads and which are reconstruction.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The final matchstick pattern.</b> The five-cell display was sampled every second from 6:24 to 7:12 and the cells never held still: separate passes over the same frame read the digits differently, and the digit count itself flipped between four and five depending on which crop we used. With a diagonal match sitting in the last cell, a confident transcription is not possible. This page therefore prints no digit string for the box-lid puzzle. The calculator's <b>17760</b> is solid — that was read twice off the LCD itself — but we did not watch it being entered into the display.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The ending and the reward.</b> The upload is 8:43 long, but the file we decoded stops at <b>7:12</b> — the container's last packet is at 432.2 seconds and everything after it is unrecoverable. So there is no results card, no <i>level completed</i> screen and no coin reward in our source. This page prints no reward figure for Kids Bedroom 1, and any number you see elsewhere is not from this recording.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The answers to the knob, track and tangram puzzles.</b> We can describe all three confidently — six animal knobs, a red-green-orange track with puzzle tabs, a fish silhouette filled with red and blue triangles — but the footage never holds a clean "solved" frame for long enough to read a state off it. Rather than publish a guessed knob order or triangle placement, those sections stay descriptive.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The significance of the 4 on the box's side panel.</b> The <b>74</b> is used: 240 × 74 = 17,760 is what the calculator lands on. The <b>4</b> on the right-hand panel is read just as reliably, but nothing in the decodable part of the recording uses it. It may belong to a later step in the level, or to the box's own lid puzzle. We are not going to invent a sum for it.
    </div>
